{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And YHWH said.</b> Many have stumbled because they found \"from the midst of the fire you heard His words\" (Deuteronomy 4:36) — which was at Mount Sinai, for it is written \"and YHWH descended upon Mount Sinai, to the top of the mountain\" (above 19:20) — yet now He says, \"from the heavens I have spoken with you.\" Whoever has a heart will understand the reason in the section Ki Tissa. Only now I shall give you a parable; perhaps even one who has no heart will understand. Suppose there is the likeness of a man whose head is in the heavens and whose feet are on Mount Sinai. This is the meaning of \"and He descended\" and \"from the heavens He will speak,\" like \"and His feet shall stand on that day upon the Mount of Olives\" (Zechariah 14:4), for we know that the heavens and the earth are full of His glory."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:36:27.400056249Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}